> Work with the hitboxes of blocks and entities.

name Hitbox
slug bookshelf-hitbox
version 5.0.0
tags runtime
authors Aksiome

$blocks: #[id(registry="function",tags="allowed")] string > [block provider](#block-providers), such as `#bs.hitbox:get_block/collision`
$entities: #[id(registry="function",tags="allowed")] string > [entity provider](#entity-providers), such as `#bs.hitbox:get_entity/sized`

$get_block:
  @position > position of the block
  output result: int @ 0..1 > `1` if the block has a shape, `0` otherwise
  output storage: int @ 1..15 | [[double] @ 7]
  > the flags of a full block, or its boxes as `[[x1,y1,z1,x2,y2,z2,flag],...]`, from the min corner to the max corner, measured in blocks from the lowest corner of the block
  >
  > Bookshelf providers flag the block `1` and its fluid `2`

$kind[living]:
  since: 2026/09/29 26.3
  get: Get the box of an entity that has health, such as mobs, players and armor stands.
  test: is living
  all: Entities that have health, such as mobs, players and armor stands.

$kind[pushable]:
  since: 2026/09/28 26.3
  get: Get the box of an entity others bump into or push, such as boats and mobs.
  test: is pushable
  all: Entities others bump into or push, such as boats and mobs.

$kind[sized]:
  since: 2023/11/21 1.20.3
  get: Get the box of any entity that has one.
  test: has a box
  all: Entities that have a box, such as mobs, items and projectiles.

$kind[solid]:
  since: 2026/09/28 26.3
  get: Get the box of an entity others can't pass through, such as boats and shulkers.
  test: is solid
  all: Entities others can't pass through, such as boats and shulkers.

$kind[targetable]:
  since: 2026/09/28 26.3
  get: Get the box of an entity a player can target, such as mobs and item frames.
  test: can be targeted
  all: Entities a player can target, such as mobs and item frames.


feature function get_block/collision > Get the collision of a block: the boxes entities can't pass through.
  since 2025/08/27 1.21.8
  $get_block

feature function get_block/collision_with_fluid > Get the collision of a block and of its fluid.
  since 2025/10/07 1.21.10
  $get_block

feature function get_block/interaction > Get the outline of a block as the game uses it to place blocks: a hollow block such as a cauldron or a hopper counts as full, so aiming into it places against it.
  since 2025/11/11 1.21.10
  $get_block

feature function get_block/interaction_with_fluid > Get the outline of a block as the game uses it to place blocks, and its fluid.
  since 2025/11/11 1.21.10
  $get_block

feature function get_block/outline > Get the outline of a block: the boxes where it can be targeted.
  since 2025/08/27 1.21.8
  $get_block

feature function get_block/outline_with_fluid > Get the outline of a block and of its fluid.
  since 2025/10/07 1.21.10
  $get_block

feature function get_entity/$kind > $kind.get
  since $kind.since
  @executor > entity to get the box of
  output result: int @ 0..1 > `1` if the entity $kind.test, `0` otherwise
  output storage: [[float] @ 7]
  > the boxes of the entity as `[[x1,y1,z1,x2,y2,z2,flag],...]`, from the min corner to the max corner, measured in blocks from the position of the entity, with its scale applied
  >
  > Bookshelf providers flag every box `1`

feature function is_in_block > Check if a position is inside a block.
  since 2023/11/21 1.20.3
  @position > position to check
  input storage
    blocks: $blocks
  output success > whether the position is inside the block

feature function is_in_entity > Check if a position is inside an entity.
  since 2023/11/21 1.20.3
  @executor > entity to check
  @position > position to check
  input storage
    entities: $entities
  output success > whether the position is inside the entity

feature function overlaps/block > Check if an entity overlaps the block at a position.
  since 2024/09/28 1.21
  @executor > entity to check
  @position > position of the block
  input storage
    blocks: $blocks
    entities: $entities
  output success > whether the entity overlaps a block

feature function overlaps/blocks > Check if an entity overlaps any block around it.
  since 2025/03/10 1.21.4
  @executor > entity to check
  input storage
    blocks: $blocks
    entities: $entities
  output success > whether the entity overlaps a block

feature block_tag has_fluid > Blocks that hold a fluid in every state, such as water, lava and kelp; waterloggable blocks hold one when their waterlogged state is true.
  since 2026/09/29 26.3

feature block_tag has_no_collision > Blocks with no collision in any of their states, such as flowers and buttons.
  since 2025/01/24 1.21.4

feature block_tag has_no_outline > Blocks with no outline to target, such as air, light blocks and fluids.
  since 2024/09/28 1.21

feature block_tag has_shape_offset > Blocks whose outline and collision move with their position, such as flowers, bamboo and pointed dripstone.
  since 2025/08/27 1.21.8

feature block_tag has_visual_offset > Blocks whose model moves with their position, such as flowers, grass and ferns.
  since 2025/08/27 1.21.8

feature block_tag is_full_cube_collision > Blocks whose collision is a full cube in every state.
  since 2026/08/11 26.2

feature block_tag is_full_cube_outline > Blocks whose outline is a full cube in every state.
  since 2026/08/11 26.2

feature block_tag is_liquid > Liquid blocks, whose level sets the height of their fluid: water and lava.
  since 2026/09/29 26.3

feature block_tag is_waterloggable > Blocks that can be waterlogged, holding water when their waterlogged state is true, such as slabs and stairs.
  since 2025/11/11 1.21.10

feature predicate get_entity/$kind > $kind.all
  since 2026/09/29 26.3
  @executor > entity to test
  output success > whether the provider may return a box for it
